{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/39412-the-scion-hunger-games-tri-wizard-cup-tournament","id":39412,"title":"The Scion \"Hunger Games/Tri-Wizard Cup\" Tournament...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-30T08:47:50-08:00","id":39412,"title":"The Scion \"Hunger Games/Tri-Wizard Cup\" Tournament...","content":"Okay, so since I've been getting so much great feedback on my Birthrights Suggestions thread, I thought I'd ask for some advice on how to flesh out the storyline I'm working with for this game.<br /> <br /> I already mentioned the basic plot of the story in the Suggestions thread, but here it is in summary.<br /> <br /> This story is set in a World where the Titans have not yet escaped. This is more of a &quot;peacetime&quot; setting. Scions exist in large numbers. It's more of a Percy Jackson kind of world. Scions from all over the world learn about their powers and responsibilities at a special school maintained by their respective pantheons. Every year, all the schools choose a single Scion as their champion and these champions compete against the champions of the other schools in a competition that closely resembles the Hunger Games. Unlike the Hunger Games, however, Scions are there on a voluntary basis, and killing every other Scion is not the goal of the contest. Like the Hunger Games, the victorious champion is richly rewarded by his/her pantheon. The Gods themselves don't really gain anything except for bragging rights when their champion wins, not to mention a lot of gods probably do a fair bit of wagering on the outcome.<br /> <br /> The Game resembles the Hunger Games in the sense of the Gods create an isolated, challenging environment for the champions, full of traps, captured Titanspawn, and other hazards in which the Scions will compete. As I said, killing is NOT the central goal of the Game. If it was, then only the combat-oriented Scions would ever get chosen to compete. You just don't send a Scion of Aphrodite into a &quot;to the death&quot; battle against Scions of Tyr, Hachiman, Horus, etc. No the idea behind this Game is more of a &quot;Capture the Flag&quot; kind of deal. Somewhere on the island, there is a &quot;Golden MacGuffin&quot; and victory is achieved by finding the Golden MacGuffin, acquiring it, and bringing it back to your pantheon's base. This allows for a wide range of possible victory scenarios that allow Scions of every stripe to successfully compete.<br /> <br /> Now, Scions can and do die in this competition. As I said, the environment is designed to be hostile to the champions. Scions can be killed by deadly traps, or eaten by monsters, or killed by some environmental mishap. Also? While killing your competition isn't a victory scenario, killing isn't EXPLICITLY forbidden in the rules. Scions CAN kill each other, it just isn't a guarantee of victory to do so. One obvious thing to be mindful of is the Teotl Scion. He/she always has the option to sacrifice an opposing Scion for a quick Legend recharge. If you do kill an opposing Scion, you will have to deal with the fact that that Scion's divine parent (not to mention his/her entire pantheon) is going to be PISSED at you. Not to mention, once word gets around to the other champions that you are killing your competition, what do you think they're going to do if THEY encounter you? They're probably going to decide that they need to kill you before you kill them. So killing is permitted, but not a great idea. There are already several ways you can end up dead in this competition as it is.<br /> <br /> Also like the Hunger Games, Scions can improve their chances for victory by attempting to win &quot;sponsors&quot; from the Gods. The more the Gods like you, the more likely they are to aid you. The rules forbid the Gods from intervening TOO directly, but they can do things to help you out. No, Zeus can't strike the Aesir champion with a bolt of lightning, but he CAN summon up a sudden thunderstorm to make climbing a mountain much more hazardous for him. No, Tyr can't personally come down and beat the crap out of the Scion of Horus, but he COULD dispatch a squad of einherjar to support the Aesir champion. The Scion of Odin is running short of Legend points? Poof! One of Idun's golden apples appears next to him. The Scion of Horus has the Golden MacGuffin and is making his way back to the Netjer's base, but the Scion of Zeus is in hot pursuit? Bam! Geb raises an earth wall to slow him down. Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Obviously this aid may not necessarily be free. If a god aids you (especially if you win because of it) he/she can easily approach you later and demand a favor for the assist. Some gods may help without thought of recompense, but others won't. Also? Gods CAN aid champions from outside their pantheon. So the Scion of Nuada thought that timely assist came from the Dagda? Nope. Turns out it was Set.....and now he/she owes this foreign god a debt. <br /> <br /> All Scions in this competition are starting out at Legend 5 to allow for some good use of Boons and Knacks to keep things interesting. Each pantheon has one champion only. The competition does not end until one Scion brings the Golden MacGuffin back to his/her base. Yes, this means that a sneaky Scion may just remain in hiding until he/she sees one of the other champions nearing his/her base with the MacGuffin, bash that champion over the head, snatch the MacGuffin and run like Hel (see what I did there ;P) back to his/her OWN base. Also like the Hunger Games, champions can form alliances with each other at will. The obvious understanding being that these alliances are short term. Champions can break their alliances at any time, whether by simply agreeing to go their separate ways or by suddenly turning on each other at a critical moment.<br /> <br /> So, that's the basic premise. My players are already working on their own characters. I will be working on various NPCs to represent the other champions from pantheons that no one claimed. I don't have a specific plan for who should win and who should lose. I just want my players to have some fun knowing that they can do basically ANYTHING to attempt to win this thing. Including fighting each other and/or backstabbing each other if they wish. I'm also thinking I'm going to want to draw up a map of the island so I can decide what they encounter and when.<br /> <br /> Do any of you have any suggestions that I may not have thought of yet? Any rules I may want to add to the competition? Any advice on NPCs I might want to design? Any specific ideas for challenges to put in front of the champions? Any advice on what the &quot;Golden MacGuffin&quot; should actually be? Any advice on stories that may spin off from this Game?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T09:26:26-08:00","id":39433,"title":"","content":"An interesting premise! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I have some questions, namely: which Pantheons are participating, and have your players decided which they will be representing?<br /> <br /> Also, it might just be me, but raising a wall of Earth to stop an opposing Scion sounds like the very definition of acting directly! Might I suggest that, instead, it work more like the Hunger Games, in the sense that your sponsor can helpyou, but he can't hinder an opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T09:49:17-08:00","id":39456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/39412-the-scion-hunger-games-tri-wizard-cup-tournament?p=39433#post39433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting premise! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I have some questions, namely: which Pantheons are participating, and have your players decided which they will be representing?<br /> <br /> Also, it might just be me, but raising a wall of Earth to stop an opposing Scion sounds like the very definition of acting directly! Might I suggest that, instead, it work more like the Hunger Games, in the sense that your sponsor can helpyou, but he can't hinder an opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the Pantheons represented in Gotham By Night are being represented at the Game. That includes the Aesir, the Annuna, the Bogovi, the Deva, the Netjer, the Orisha, the Teotl, the Theoi, the Tuatha, the Yazata, the Kami, the Shen, and the Nemetondevos.<br /> <br /> My current players are representing the Theoi (a female Scion of Zeus), the Netjer (a son of Horus), the Annuna (a son of Ishtar), the Aesir (a son of Odin), and one player who is waffling between either the Kami (Scion of Tsuki-Yomi) or the Shen (Scion of Nuwa).<br /> <br /> Raising an earth wall isn't directly harming the opposing Scion. It's just putting up an obstacle to hinder his progress. If the Scion in question has good jumping Knacks or Wind's Freedom, it'll hardly slow him down at all. Now if Geb used Quicksand to sink the opposing Scion into the Earth, now THAT would be more of a direct attack. As would causing a massive earthquake that could potentially kill the Scion. Also, if he raised up an Earth Igloo or something to completely encase the Scion, that would also be a bit more of a direct hindrance. Just putting up and obstacle for him to overcome merely inconveniences him, it doesn't make it impossible for him to prevail.<br /> <br /> At least that's the prevailing theory anyway. Nothing's set in stone yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T10:07:39-08:00","id":39463,"title":"","content":"If you are concerned about less combat-oriented Scions being overshadowed, why not have multiple events instead of just one?<br /> <br /> I've been reading a lot of L5R books in recent times, so the tournament to become Topaz Champion strikes me as a decent example. It's famous for having an iaijutsu competition at the end, but the contestants also compete in other martial skills, a number of the arts, tests of virtue, and even matters of practical knowledge.<br /> <br /> A big capture-the-flag scenario sounds like it'd make for an exciting finish, but lead-up events could lend an extra bit of spice going into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","user":"Creticus","date":". 12-30-2013, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T10:12:00-08:00","id":39465,"title":"","content":"Ah, I'm almost a little disappointed that the pdf Pantheons aren't in, but then the Alihah Scion would have a distinct advantage with the Safa and Umrah Boons from Hajj. I'm almost feeling sorry for the Teotl Scion...s/he will be kind of at a disadvantage as the only one who can't meaningfully utilize her PSP's 4-dot power. Perhaps make her a Scion of Quetzalcoatl, who wouldn't be likely to use anything but the auto-sacrifice parts anyway?<br /> <br /> I don't think it's harming the opposing Scion. I just don't like the idea of Gods actively hindering other champions, just helping theirs. But whatever works for your game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Have you any ideas for NPC Scions yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:41:47-08:00","id":39505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/39412-the-scion-hunger-games-tri-wizard-cup-tournament?p=39463#post39463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are concerned about less combat-oriented Scions being overshadowed, why not have multiple events instead of just one?<br /> <br /> I've been reading a lot of L5R books in recent times, so the tournament to become Topaz Champion strikes me as a decent example. It's famous for having an iaijutsu competition at the end, but the contestants also compete in other martial skills, a number of the arts, tests of virtue, and even matters of practical knowledge.<br /> <br /> A big capture-the-flag scenario sounds like it'd make for an exciting finish, but lead-up events could lend an extra bit of spice going into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. A thought that just occurred to me on this front? I still need some time to draw up a map of the island anyway. Plus I could use more time to build my NPCs.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, these &quot;preliminary events&quot; you're advocating could be more like &quot;qualifying matches&quot; in which the various Pantheons put several candidates for the position of their champion against each other in order to determine who gets the job? I have been trying to hammer out how each Scion got tapped for the job, since obviously every god wants his/her kid to be the one to bring glory to their pantheon. Perhaps some preliminary competitions in which the winners move on to represent their pantheon in the &quot;main event?&quot; Sounds workable.<br /> <br /> Also, the idea of the capture-the-flag game was specifically intended to make sure that non-combat Scions DON'T get overshadowed. Yeah, a combat Scion can choose to just fight his/her way through the competition and gain the win by brute force. That's kinda what combat characters always do. But a Social Scion could succeed at a game like this simply by manipulating people into helping him/her. Or he/she could seduce one of the combat monsters into being his/her protector. Or he/she could sow dissent to break up alliances. A more Mental Scion could engineer elaborate traps to ensnare his/her competition. Or he/she could use his/her Purviews in ways that can stymie the others. Epic Intelligence + Forest Environment + Fertility Purview = HOLY SHIT!<br /> <br /> But yeah, some preliminary competitions may be an interesting way to prolong the competition. We're mostly playing this game to kill time until Exalted 3rd Edition or Scion 2e comes out. Whichever comes first. So letting this run a reasonably long time may be a good idea after all. It was, after all, almost certainly the Theoi who probably first came up with this Game idea. It obviously bears some striking resemblance to the Olympic Games as well. And the Olympics always feature multiple events. So yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:49:42-08:00","id":39508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/39412-the-scion-hunger-games-tri-wizard-cup-tournament?p=39465#post39465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I'm almost a little disappointed that the pdf Pantheons aren't in, but then the Alihah Scion would have a distinct advantage with the Safa and Umrah Boons from Hajj. I'm almost feeling sorry for the Teotl Scion...s/he will be kind of at a disadvantage as the only one who can't meaningfully utilize her PSP's 4-dot power. Perhaps make her a Scion of Quetzalcoatl, who wouldn't be likely to use anything but the auto-sacrifice parts anyway?<br /> <br /> I don't think it's harming the opposing Scion. I just don't like the idea of Gods actively hindering other champions, just helping theirs. But whatever works for your game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Have you any ideas for NPC Scions yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was worried about the Teotl Scion as well. Perhaps he/she WILL be a Scion of Quetzalcoatl......or another thing to remember is that there WILL be captured Titanspawn in this arena as well. The Teotl Scion could easily use Itzli 4 on one of them without a problem.<br /> <br /> You might actually be right about directly hindering an opposing Scion. The real problem I've been coming up with is where does one draw the line? Yeah, putting up an obstacle in front of an opponent is harmless enough. But another Earth god might make the argument that then he/she should be able to use Quicksand to sink an opposing Scion. Yeah, as I said, Sky gods would be specifically forbidden from striking an enemy Scion with a lightning bolt. But what about triggering a big gust of wind while an opposing Scion is scaling a mountain?<br /> <br /> I suppose an important distinction to make is that the Gods can also move to rescue their Scions if they get into too much trouble. Yeah, if Zeus blows another champion off a mountain, that champion's Pantheon is well within their rights to take measures to insure that their champion isn't killed or seriously injured from the fall. Maybe THEIR Sky god conjures up a wind to stop the fall, and then lifts the Scion back to where he/she was in the first place.<br /> <br /> These are definitely things to think about.<br /> <br /> I haven't had much time to come up with NPC champions just yet, I'm afraid. That's one thing I'm going to have to make a priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T14:21:01-08:00","id":39591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/39412-the-scion-hunger-games-tri-wizard-cup-tournament?p=39505#post39505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, these &quot;preliminary events&quot; you're advocating could be more like &quot;qualifying matches&quot; in which the various Pantheons put several candidates for the position of their champion against each other in order to determine who gets the job? I have been trying to hammer out how each Scion got tapped for the job, since obviously every god wants his/her kid to be the one to bring glory to their pantheon. Perhaps some preliminary competitions in which the winners move on to represent their pantheon in the &quot;main event?&quot; Sounds workable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly one way to do it.<br /> <br /> I was thinking something more along the lines of separate competitions with separate prizes, some of which are meant for prestige and some of which can be used in the main event. For example, winning the shooting contest means that the winner has the right to call for a thunderbolt to the Scion of his or her choice during the main event, while winning the philosophical debate hosted by Xi Wangmu means receiving one of her peaches of immortality. Meanwhile, in between the events, the Scions would be cutting deals, making friends, and seeing the spectacle that a bunch of celebratory gods can throw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:33:48-08:00","id":53974,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I've managed to hammer out most of the details for this Game, and now I'm doing some thinking about what to do for a follow-up. I've been trying to contemplate what kind of stories could spin off from the Game, and I think I've got something. Tell me what you think.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I've been playing with the idea of having the competition of the Games kind of spill over into a potentially larger inter-Pantheon conflict. My idea here is a bit of a variation on how the Trojan War got started. So, as I said from the beginning, the victorious Scion in these Games is richly rewarded by the Gods. I'm thinking the Games are celebrated by a victory feast wherein the other Champions and other Pantheons are expected to pay at least a little homage to the Scion (and by extension, his/her Pantheon) who actually won the competition. At some point during the feast, the Victor (may as well use Hunger Games terms, since it inspired this idea) enjoys a special treat........a golden apple.<br /> <br /> As soon as the Victor eats the apple, several Gods and Goddesses pretty much instantaneously falls in love with the Victor. Who specifically is affected will be customized according to whoever it is who actually wins. The important thing is that several Gods and Goddesses (all of them from other Pantheons) suddenly want this Victor in the worst way. Fighting erupts. Eventually one of the affected Gods/Goddesses manages to grab the Victor and run off with him/her. A huge scandal erupts. The other affected Gods want to reclaim the Victor for themselves. The unaffected Gods are still outraged by this massive breach of etiquette. Tensions start to build. Pantheons start preparing for war. My player's Band are charged with the task of trying to defuse the situation. They can either try to help calm tensions, they can attempt to rescue the Victor (which may involve a directive from an affected divine parent to return the Victor to him/her), or they can investigate the root cause of this situation.<br /> <br /> Now, I know this sounds like it's been done before...and that's the point. Sooner or later, someone comes to his/her senses and goes &quot;Hey, wait a minute! A golden apple comes into play and suddenly we're all at each other's throats over one person? Why does this seem so familiar? ERIS!&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I'm still trying to iron out the particulars, but I don't want it to be THAT obvious. I kind of like the idea that Eris may actually have nothing to do with this incident. The idea of Eris being framed is kind of amusing to me. So, for a twist, I thought it would be fun to reveal that someone else may have set this up. Perhaps more than one &quot;someone else.&quot; Or, if Eris is, in fact, involved, then she isn't operating alone and there's some larger effort underway here. What exactly that is, I can't really say right now.<br /> <br /> So, what do you all think? How would you run something like this? What advice do you have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}